From 5dc93e463bf41f35c3ff15ec3339740bfecd1f43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:09:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] thingino-lensd: AF feed, ONVIF PTZ, serial IR-cut,
 Pelco-D (lensd -P)

For PTZ cameras built around a serial lens/PTZ board. lensd feeds the AF
board two focus values a frame from the ISP's AF statistics, with the
vendor's AF window and filter; lensctl is the ONVIF PTZ backend (continuous
pan/tilt/zoom, presets, home); the lens head's IR-cut is switched over serial,
following ric's day/night pins (read from raptor.conf) from ric's state at
start; and -P speaks plain Pelco-D to heads with no AF feed.

The heads have no pan/tilt position feedback, so RelativeMove is a timed
move: lensctl rel times each axis from the head's measured speed at each
Pelco-D level (heads/<head>.conf; the JL12D2's head is measured), one axis
after the other, and lensd holds "moving" from the first frame to the stop,
which is what Frigate's autotracking waits on. A head with no calibration
gets no RelativeMove.

Every SigmaStar board builds it. A choice, BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_LENSD_MODE
(off, af or pelco), is written to /etc/default/lensd, with the head's name
(BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_LENSD_HEAD); in off lensd does not run, and the ONVIF
PTZ files, the head files and the web UI plugin are not installed.
